{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788132865,"nonce":"0ojd2btATVtYeCYSp3WBfGISmlA=","message":"AMENDMENT from the action-surface audit — orchestrator, session 4.\n\n**Designators the scope list omits.** 12 of the 25 right-click reverse\ndesignators (`Verse/ReverseDesignatorDatabase.cs:43-77`) plus ~20 architect ones\nare absent. Ranked by when they bite:\n\n- **`Claim` — M1.** `RimWorld/Designator_Claim.cs:53-69`. This is how you take\n  ancient-ruins furniture and abandoned buildings. Without it the agent cannot\n  use anything it did not build.\n- **`Install` / reinstall a minified thing — M2**, and it belongs to 3.3 rather\n  than here: `RimWorld/Designator_Install.cs:116`. Moving furniture without\n  rebuilding it.\n- `MineVein` (`:66`) — mines a whole ore vein from ONE designate, cheaper than\n  painting cells.\n- `SmoothSurface` / `SmoothFloors` / `SmoothWalls`, `RemovePaint`,\n  `RemoveFloor` (`:50`) / `RemoveFoundation`\n- `ReleaseAnimalToWild` (`:53`), `ExtractTree` (`:59`) / `Replant`,\n  `ExtractSkull` (`:81`), `EjectFuel` (`:36`), `FillIn` (`:39`),\n  `DeconstructConduit` (`:20`)\n- Roof areas: `AreaBuildRoof` (`:38`) / `AreaNoRoof` (`:45`) / `AreaIgnoreRoof` (`:37`)\n- `AreaSnowClear`, `AreaPollutionClear`, `ZoneAdd_Fishing` (Odyssey — the bench\n  runs it)\n- Biotech `Adopt` / `MechControlGroup` — out of scope per DESIGN's new DLC\n  non-goal, listed so the omission is deliberate rather than accidental.\n\n**A `flick` verb is missing and its shape is unusual.** `CompFlickable` adds a\nFlick DESIGNATION (`RimWorld/CompFlickable.cs:113-124`) — same designation\nmanager this spec already drives for forbid/unforbid/cancel, but reached through\na per-thing gizmo toggle rather than a cell-drag designator. Power on/off is\ntherefore ASYNCHRONOUS: `SwitchIsOn` (`:38`) does not move until a colonist\nwalks over. Also raised on 3.4; wherever it lands, echo the designation, not the\nstate.\n\n**Zone scope gaps.** Growing zones have `allowSow` (`RimWorld/Zone_Growing.cs:154-165`)\nand `allowCut` (`:166-175`) toggles the scope does not mention, and hydroponics\nbasins are a separate `Building_PlantGrower` (`:43`) with the same \"what to grow\"\nsetting. The curriculum audit adds a doctrine point worth encoding: **a growing\nzone with no plant set grows nothing**, which is why the scripted tutorial names\nrice explicitly — `zone add growing` should refuse or warn without `--plant`.\n\n**Storage settings are NOT in this spec** — they moved to the new 3.6 (48f666c)\nwith bills, because `Zone_Stockpile` and `Building_Storage` share one\n`IStoreSettingsParent` API and splitting them across two specs would split one\ntrap (a grouped `Building_Storage.GetStoreSettings()` returns the GROUP's object,\n`RimWorld/Building_Storage.cs:100`). This spec still creates and shapes the\nzones; 3.6 owns what they accept and at what priority.","files":null}]}